The "Grendel" is a small, cheap ($150), high-capacity (12 rounds)
pistol chambered for the .380 round (that's a reasonaable power
ammo for a small, concealable pistol).  It is made in Florida, and has
a synthetic grip (like the Glock).  HOWEVER, it is picky about
the ammo that is will reliably use without jamming.  You must be
willing to experiment with different ammo until you find some that
reliably feeds.

For a very cheap pocket gun with moderate power and high capacity it
is a good choice.  I bought one because I have a .45 that is a bit too
large to carry all the time.  I can keep the Grendel in my coat
pocket, and, if necessary in a pinch, even shoot through the pocket.

Eventually I want to get a Seecamp (sp?), which a fellow Huntsville
Extropian owns.  It's a tiny stainless pocket pistol in .32 that holds
7 rounds.  But it costs > $400, and is hard to get, so the Grendel
will do for now.

