Subject: GUNS: Glock's, etc.

Edgar Swank wrote:

> In my quick look at a Glock (I was in a hurry & wasn't going to buy a
> pistol that day) I thought I saw a small vertical slider sticking up
> out of a slightly longer slot on the left side which I thought would
> be the safety.  It was quite small, with a few serrations on top.
> Looked like it would be good for breaking your fingernail on.  Was
> that something other than the safety?

That's a gadget used in the takedown of the gun, that is, for
disassembling the slide. Far too small to be a safety, in any case.
Safety levers are largish and easily reached, in almost modern guns.

The Glock "Safe Action" is the trigger pull itself, with a minor
addition to the trigger that I cannot hope to describe in words here.
If you examine a Glock carefully, you'll understand how it works.

> Please, everyone, keep posting info on pistols.  I would also like to
> join the "Bargainmiester" in requesting more info on lower-priced
> pistols.

Glocks can be gotten for about $400...how much cheaper do you want to
go?

A used .357 magnum revolver (lots of them, as police forces switched
to semiautos) can probably be gotten for $250. Check out the display
case of nearly any gun store (e.g., for Edgar, try "Sportsman's
Supply").

A worn .38 or .357 might be had for $200, but that's about as low as
it gets given the value of today's dollar.


